2026-10-22T10:32:00Z  CHANGE   Closed by the same rewrite as T0153: encodeAudio resamples the whole batch once into a scratch frame in the encoder's own format and cuts whole encoder frames out of a per-plane FIFO. No per-frame allocation or full-tail shift remains; the residual erase is one frame's bytes per emitted frame.
2026-10-22T10:32:00Z  CHANGE   The stride is no longer one number for both sides. The input frame count is buffer.size() / channels, where channels describes the queue's layout (AudioQueue stores stereo after its own conversion, so VideoRecorderThread passing 2 is the input truth, not a guess about the encoder). The output side comes from the scratch frame: audioCodecCtx_->ch_layout.nb_channels and audioCodecCtx_->sample_fmt, via appendPending and av_samples_copy. A mono encoder is therefore described by its own layout rather than by the caller's channel count.
